On Wednesday 05 November 2003 20:49, hfroark wrote:
> Actually, I think that there is a problem. If I am not missing a
> point, Lojban words inculding type-4 fu'ivla have to begin with a
> consonant or (mandatory) pause. So, "angeli" should be ".angeli", or
> the other changes including "xangeli" would also work.

Yes, a word beginning with a vowel must be preceded by a pause, but it doesn't 
have to be written. It's better to write it, though.

It is even possible, though hard to read, to omit all spaces in a sequence 
consisting of cmavo, all except possibly the first beginning with consonants 
and none containing 'y', and possibly one brivla beginning with a consonant 
at the end: {ilezdani belebarda angeli cublanu}.

